HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

Governance, Protocols and Services filled in for real; minimal Kernel implemented and tested.

WHY

Validating the repository before building the Kernel surfaced two real
gaps against the Dependency Graph the project itself uses to order its
own construction: Kernel depends on `contracts` and `services`, but
`services/` still held only a purpose README. Separately, `ontology` and
`contracts` had already been written against `governance` and `protocols`
while those two also still held only purpose READMEs — a retroactive
dependency gap. Both needed closing before Kernel could honestly be
called unblocked.

DECISION

Wrote governance/GOVERNANCE_PROTOCOL_0.1.0.pdl (abstract, name-free:
a root authority role exists, decisions must be traceable, history is
permanent, every artifact is a versioned object, a request only binds
once promoted) and protocols/PDL_SPECIFICATION_0.1.0.pdl (the minimal
flat KEY-VALUE-per-line grammar sufficient to read/write a .pace/
instance's root manifest files — deliberately scoped to that, not the
richer nested prose style this repository's own governance/ontology/
contracts documents use).

Implemented services/pdl.py (parses that grammar) and services/fs.py
(generic upward directory search, the mechanism Kernel uses to locate
.pace/ the way Git locates .git/).

Implemented kernel/kernel.py: locate_instance() walks upward for a
.pace/ directory; validate_instance() checks it structurally against
contracts/INSTANCE_CONTRACT_0.1.0.pdl — required fields in INSTANCE.pdl
and ACTIVE_VERSIONS.pdl, ORG_REF required when KIND=PROJECT, SCHEMA_VERSION
against a supported set, all 11 required sections present, history/
non-empty, and no code/script file anywhere inside .pace/. Deliberately
does not attempt semantic validation — that stays the future Doctor
engine's job.

Built a fixture minimal valid instance under kernel/tests/fixtures/
example_instance/.pace/ and a smoke test (kernel/tests/test_kernel.py,
no external test framework dependency) covering: locate from inside the
instance, locate from a nested subdirectory, a valid fixture reporting
zero violations, a missing INSTANCE.pdl being caught, and an unsupported
SCHEMA_VERSION being caught. All 5 assertions verified passing before
this commit, plus a manual end-to-end run of kernel.py's own entrypoint
against the fixture.

IMPACT

The Dependency Graph's own rule ("consult it before building any
component, confirm dependencies have real content, not just a README")
was actually followed here, not skipped for momentum's sake. Kernel is
now real, tested code — not a design document — and is the first PACE
component with actual behavior.

NEXT_STEPS

Per the roadmap: a minimal CLI wrapping the Kernel, then pace init, then
adopting TuPeríMetro as the first governed project.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
